{"claims":[{"excerpt":"De James Webb-ruimtetelescoop moest opgevouwen in de Ariane 5-raket passen.","claim":"Webb was designed to fold so it would fit inside the Ariane 5 rocket.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb was designed to fold into a compact launch configuration that fit inside the Ariane 5.","narrative":"Webb moest compact in de Ariane 5-raket passen, hoewel zijn operationele configuratie daarvoor te groot was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source confirms Webb was designed to fold into a compact configuration that fit inside the Ariane 5.","materiality":"Relevant context for why deployment was necessary."},{"excerpt":"In de ruimte moest hij zich vervolgens uitvouwen tot zijn operationele configuratie","claim":"After launch, Webb had to unfold in space to reach its operational configuration.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"In the two weeks after launch, the entire observatory underwent a highly choreographed transformation—unfurling, extending and expanding to a configuration that is very different to how it looks when stored inside the rocket for liftoff.","narrative":"De uitvouwing bracht de telescoop in de tweede week in die configuratie","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source describes the observatory unfolding after launch and reaching its fully deployed operational configuration.","materiality":"Central to the deployment timeline."},{"excerpt":"een reeks stappen met mogelijke faalpunten.","claim":"Deployment involved multiple steps with possible points of failure.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"There were over 50 major deployment steps, with 178 release mechanisms that had to perform perfectly or any one of over 300 single points of failure could have diminished or crippled the mission.","narrative":"De uitvouwing omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten, waardoor duidelijk is dat dit een risicovolle fase was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source documents many deployment steps and more than 300 possible single points of failure. The piece does not imply that any failure occurred.","materiality":"Conveys the stakes of deployment."},{"excerpt":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld.","claim":"By the second week, the mirrors themselves had unfolded and latched.","category":"technical","label":"F1 minor immaterial imprecision","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures by unfolding and latching the secondary mirror tripod and rotating and latching the two primary mirror wings.","narrative":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source specifies that the secondary-mirror tripod unfolded and latched and the primary-mirror wings rotated and latched; describing this as the mirrors unfolding is shorthand for deploying their supporting structures.","materiality":"A technical distinction, but it does not change the stated deployment outcome or timeline."},{"excerpt":"Webb had zijn operationele vorm bereikt","claim":"Webb reached its fully deployed operational configuration in the second week.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"De uitvouwing bracht de telescoop in de tweede week in die configuratie","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly says the second-week deployment brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","materiality":"Establishes when deployment was complete."},{"excerpt":"en de uitvouwing was soepel verlopen.","claim":"Webb's deployment proceeded smoothly.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's deployment was completed with remarkable smoothness.","narrative":"de uitvouwing verliep soepel.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source characterizes deployment as remarkably smooth.","materiality":"Rules out an implication that later commissioning addressed a deployment failure."},{"excerpt":"Maar uitgevouwen zijn was niet hetzelfde als klaar zijn voor routinewetenschap.","claim":"Reaching the deployed configuration did not mean Webb was ready for routine science operations.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments. ... After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"maar was niet hetzelfde als klaar voor routinewetenschap","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source distinguishes completion of deployment from the subsequent commissioning work before routine operations began.","materiality":"This is the piece's central distinction."},{"excerpt":"Daarna volgden weken van afkoeling, maanden van spiegeluitlijning en de kalibratie van de instrumenten.","claim":"After deployment, Webb underwent weeks of cooling, months of mirror alignment, and instrument calibration.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The telescope and scientific instruments started to cool rapidly ... but it took several weeks for them to cool all the way down and reach stable temperatures. ... In the second, third and fourth months: Initial optics checkouts, and telescope alignment. ... In the fifth and sixth months: Calibration and completion of commissioning.","narrative":"Daarna volgden weken van afkoeling, maanden van spiegeluitlijning en vervolgens instrumentkalibratie.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source gives this commissioning sequence: several weeks of cooling, alignment in months two through four, and calibration in months five and six.","materiality":"Clarifies that substantial work remained after deployment."},{"excerpt":"Pas na zes maanden ingebruikname begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","claim":"Webb began routine science operations after six months of commissioning.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places the start of routine science operations after six months of commissioning.","materiality":"Provides the endpoint of the timeline."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing was een belangrijke mijlpaal, niet het einde van de weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties.","claim":"Deployment was an important milestone but not the end of Webb's path to science operations.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration. ... The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments. ... After six months: “Science operations!”","narrative":"uitgevouwen zijn een belangrijke mijlpaal was, niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source documents deployment followed by five more months of commissioning before routine science operations.","materiality":"Summarizes the distinction supported by the source timeline."}]}

